    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d151">

                <pb facs="0183" n="109" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg109"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 868.00/126</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Droppers</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Athens</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-24T20:00:00+02:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 24, 1917, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received June 25, 7.30 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>366. Venizelos and some members of his
                    cabinet now in Piraeus Harbor. <hi rendition="#italic">Pourparlers</hi> going on
                    between them and Zaimis Government
                    concerning terms of reconciliation for union of Greece. Reported that Zaimis will resign as he finds certain terms
                    unacceptable, particularly that the Venizelist Chamber of Deputies of June,
                    1915, should be convoked. Venizelos
                    maintains that present Chamber of Deputies elected January, 1916, is
                    illegal.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Droppers</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
